$ gragas help nothing
--- stdout
Unknown help topic [`nothing`]
Usage:
  gragas [flags]
  gragas [command]

Available Commands:
  attention   List what needs the owner's attention first
  bind        Bind a rule to the tool setting that holds it
  cache       List or clear what gragas keeps in its cache
  check       Validate the rulebook tree
  conflicts   List rules whose settings disagree and offer the three resolutions
  contract    Check documents, read fields, write a fixture
  coverage    List the rules tools hold and those none hold
  decision    Record a decision or supersede one, with a history entry for each change
  explain     Explain a rule or a tool entry by what holds it
  gen         Regenerate the generated files
  guard       Refuse a hand edit of a lifecycle field
  help        Help about any command
  history     List the history of a rule or of the rulebook
  import      Bring a guide and a tool's config in as rules, grandfathering what the config holds
  init        Set up a project or a rulebook
  journal     List, recover or restore runs that wrote here
  migrate     Move a rulebook to the format this build reads
  plugin      Prove, list, approve, add or upgrade a plugin, or say which contract this gragas speaks
  preset      Write every tool's preset from the rulebook's bindings
  rebind      Move a rule's binding to another tool setting
  resolve     List the rulebook a chain resolves to, and where each entry came from
  rule        Add or change a rule, with its history
  source      Record or change a source, with its history
  term        Add, change or retire a term, with its history
  tools       List the tools the rules bind to
  unbind      Remove a rule's binding
  undo        Take back the last change the history records, with a new entry
  validate    Check a rulebook and list what is wrong in it
  version     Print this build

Flags:
      --accessible      Plain questions (ACCESSIBLE)
      --config string   The settings file (GRAGAS_CONFIG)
      --json            Answer in one JSON document
      --no-color        No colour (NO_COLOR)
      --plain           Print plainly: nothing moves

Use "gragas [command] --help" for more information about a command.
--- stderr
--- exit 0
